*.local

# Env — credentials never enter git (#4's stated prerequisite). Runtime config
# for Supabase is set in Vercel's dashboard as VITE_-prefixed variables.
#
# Since #185 the file these lines exclude holds SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN, which is a
# Supabase personal access token: it authenticates as the account owner and has
# full authority over EVERY project in the account, not one. Committing it would
# be worse than committing a service-role key, which is at least scoped to a
# single project. Revoke at https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens, where
# revoking is immediate and free; `.env.example` says the rest.
#
# These two lines are not the only defence, deliberately. A `.gitignore` protects
# one path and says nothing about a token pasted into a script, a document or a
# test fixture — so `src/test/gate.test.js` scans every file in the repo, tracked
# and untracked, for a token-shaped literal. `.env.local` is correctly outside
# that scan's corpus BECAUSE these lines ignore it, which is the token's one
# sanctioned home.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

